{#- The Lenches' wording for the shared Churches page, src/_includes/pages/churches.njk. -#}
{%- set headIntro -%}<p class="page-intro">The Lenches and their neighbours are served by the ARCH Benefice, named after the parishes of <strong>A</strong>bbots Morton, <strong>R</strong>ous Lench, <strong>C</strong>hurch Lench and <strong>H</strong>arvington, which were brought together in 2001 within the Diocese of Worcester. Its churches are All Saints', Church Lench; St Peter's, Rous Lench; St James the Great, Harvington; St Peter's, Abbots Morton; and St Egwin's at Norton &amp; Lenchwick, which shares the rota though the parish formally sits in the Evesham benefice. Several other congregations are a short drive away in Evesham.</p>
    <p>All Saints' stands at the top of the hill with one of the best views in Worcestershire, looking west towards the Malverns. St Peter's at Rous Lench is unusual in having two pulpits and no fixed pews, so the space can be used flexibly.</p>
    <p>St Peter's at Abbots Morton, a Grade I listed church on the site of a Saxon one, has a 14th-century tower and a 15th-century roof whose beams are often little more than roughly shaped branches. The moated site of the abbots of Evesham's country retreat lies close by.</p>
    <p class="small"><a href="https://www.archbenefice.org.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ARCH Benefice website &rarr;</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.archbenefice.org.uk/information/arch-messenger" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the ARCH Messenger &rarr;</a></p>{%- endset -%}
{%- set servicesNote -%}<p>Services rotate around the churches, so the pattern changes from week to week. {{ services.midweek }} <span class="small muted">From the <a href="https://www.archbenefice.org.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ services.source }}</a>, updated each month.</span></p>{%- endset -%}
{%- set readingsNote -%}<p class="small muted">Each Sunday's readings link to the NRSV (Anglicised) on Bible Gateway; tap one to read it.</p>{%- endset -%}
{%- set noServices -%}<p>No service times are listed for the coming weeks yet; please check the ARCH Messenger.</p>{%- endset -%}
{%- set otherChurches -%}  <section id="evesham">
    <h2>Other congregations in Evesham</h2>
    <div class="grid">

      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="mt0">Evesham Unitarians</h3>
        <p class="mt0">Oat Street Chapel, Oat Street, Evesham WR11 4PJ. Sunday gatherings at 11am. There is a hearing loop and an accessible toilet, and the chapel conducts same-sex weddings.</p>
        <p>The building is a genuine curiosity — a remarkable survivor tucked back from the street behind the modern town centre. The hall is hired out to groups promoting dignity and respect for all, regardless of belief, gender, ability or sexual orientation.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="mt0">Evesham Methodist Church</h3>
        <p class="mt0">71 Bridge Street, Evesham WR11 4SF &middot; 01386 442380. Sunday morning worship at 10.30am, with a midweek communion on Wednesdays and a shoppers' service on Fridays.</p>
        <p>Part of the South Worcestershire Methodist Circuit, and recognised as a Church of Sanctuary.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
    <p>Both welcome visitors.</p>
  </section>

